{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00650",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.06,
      "end_seconds": 12.13,
      "duration_seconds": 10.07,
      "text": "Morning, doctor! Lovely day, isn't it? I almost cycled over, but the knee said no, so the bus it was. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.76,
      "end_seconds": 21.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.43,
      "text": "Very sensible. How is the knee, since we sent you for the scan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.45,
      "end_seconds": 34.81,
      "duration_seconds": 10.36,
      "text": "Oh, it's behaving, mostly. I've got the report here, if you want it. Though I don't understand a word of it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.27,
      "end_seconds": 45.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "Let me have it. Ah, yes. I've got the scan results up on screen too. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.02,
      "end_seconds": 51.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Go on, then, break it to me. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.52,
      "end_seconds": 67.23,
      "duration_seconds": 12.71,
      "text": "The scan is consistent with a small tear in the meniscus, which is the cartilage cushion in the knee, on the inner side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.81,
      "end_seconds": 83.4,
      "duration_seconds": 13.59,
      "text": "I thought it might be. I did my knee in at Sunday football, I told you. Twisted it in the mud, my own fault."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.63,
      "end_seconds": 92.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "And it's been how long since the twist? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.09,
      "end_seconds": 105.63,
      "duration_seconds": 9.54,
      "text": "Six weeks on Sunday. It was a daft tackle, I should know better at my age. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.22,
      "end_seconds": 117.15,
      "duration_seconds": 8.93,
      "text": "Football's a young man's game. Tell me about your tablets, so I can check against the record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.79,
      "end_seconds": 131.7,
      "duration_seconds": 11.91,
      "text": "Ibuprofen, 400 mg, when it twinges. And paracetamol, 1 gram, when the ibuprofen's not enough. I only use them after the match."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.17,
      "end_seconds": 140.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "That's sensible, and don't take more than that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.17,
      "end_seconds": 150.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.37,
      "text": "No, no, I read the packet. My wife reads it to me anyway, every time. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.82,
      "end_seconds": 162.06,
      "duration_seconds": 9.24,
      "text": "Good for her. How would you say it's been day to day, is it holding you back? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.59,
      "end_seconds": 177.14,
      "duration_seconds": 12.55,
      "text": "I can walk the dog, no bother. I just won't play for a while. The lads are gutted, mind. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.88,
      "end_seconds": 188.96,
      "duration_seconds": 9.08,
      "text": "It's early days. A small tear like this often settles with rest and strengthening exercises, without an operation. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.89,
      "end_seconds": 197.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.29,
      "text": "That's a relief. I thought you were going to say surgery. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.66,
      "end_seconds": 213.34,
      "duration_seconds": 13.68,
      "text": "Not at this stage, no. I'd like you to do the physiotherapy exercises I'll print out, daily, and avoid twisting on that leg."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.03,
      "end_seconds": 217.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Can I swim? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.85,
      "end_seconds": 226.85,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Swimming's fine, except breaststroke, which twists the knee. Front crawl is okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.13,
      "end_seconds": 234.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Right. I'm more of a doggy paddle man. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.71,
      "end_seconds": 245.4,
      "duration_seconds": 8.69,
      "text": "That'll do. Keep the knee moving, and ice it for ten minutes after exercise if it's sore. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.6,
      "end_seconds": 252.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Does that actually work? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.3,
      "end_seconds": 259.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "It can help the swelling, and it's harmless. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.98,
      "end_seconds": 267.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Fair enough. What about when I can play again? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.35,
      "end_seconds": 278.85,
      "duration_seconds": 8.5,
      "text": "Let's see how it feels in six weeks. I'd like to see you then to review it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.65,
      "end_seconds": 287.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "Six weeks. Right. Put it in the diary, would you? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.36,
      "end_seconds": 295.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Reception will do it on your way out. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.95,
      "end_seconds": 300.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Marvellous. Thanks, doc. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.82,
      "end_seconds": 306.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Mind how you go. ~"
    }
  ]
}
